key.quote:
I kan noght parfitly my pater-noster,
As the preest it syngeth;
But I kan rymes of Robyn Hood,
And Randolf erl of Chestre;

Disce, and Do-wel;
Doce, and Do-bet;
Dilige, and Do-best;

And cride mercy faste,
And wepte and wailede;
And therwith I awakede.

"It is a ful trie tree," quod he,
"Trewely to telle;
Mercy is the more therof,
The myddul stok is ruthe;

